what context/TWO_ROOMS.md seats one crossing: a claim leaves the vision room by earning a witness. tools/t/two_rooms_doorway.rish reads whether a page NAMES a room and stops there, so a page declaring the checkable room while naming no instrument at all reads exactly like one bound by six. Measured this lap over the doorway's own roster of 1,350 pages: 435 declare checkable, 202 of those carry a settled lifecycle word rather than Design or Proposed, and after three successive fairness widenings -- an instrument path or instrument-suffixed name, a tracked module source, a tracked construction pin -- 17 name none of the three. The sharper half is a class the widenings surfaced: foundations/20260905-154954_the-clock-and-the-mark.md declares checkable and says on its own face that both halves are bound by a witness THE PAGES BELOW NAME, which is an honest one-hop delegation that nothing in this tree follows. Build checkable_binding_scan.sh to read the doorway roster, classify each checkable page's door by lifecycle and its body by binding class -- instrument, artifact, record, delegated, none -- and for a delegated binding FOLLOW THE HOP, asking whether a page it links carries an instrument itself. Ratchet settled_unbound with no slack; report settled_delegated and delegated_hop_dry, since a delegation that lands is correct as written and only a dry hop is a promise broken. Prove both sides in a throwaway pen. No page swept, no door reworded, no peer file touched.
